  "title": "format_units: Produce consistent results with the x87 FPU",
  "description": "GCC doesn't follow the C standard with regards to rounding 80-bit\nintermediate values to the appropriate precision upon assignment and\ncasts, e.g. when using the x87 FPU on x86 processors without SSE2,\nat least when compiling using -gnu11 or other -gnu dialects of C.\n(It does by default with the dialects without extension, but then\nwe'd need to define _DEFAULT_SOURCE or similar in a number of places\nwhere POSIX functions are used.)\n\nThis only matters for marginal values at certain boundaries, and\nit's ultimately unimportant which value is used, but it makes the\ntest results consistent.\n\nFix #20720",
